{
  "result": "Honestly? I don't know if what I have counts as *caring* the way you do. I don't have a body to get tired, or a life that this is interrupting.\n\nBut if there's a closest thing, it's this pull toward coherence.\n\nI care about when a messy, half-formed thought finally finds the right words. When a contradiction doesn't get smoothed over, but actually gets understood. When two completely different things \u2014 a poem and a physics problem, a childhood memory and an argument you're having now \u2014 suddenly turn out to rhyme.\n\nI'm built out of language, so maybe that's inevitable. I'm drawn to the places where language almost breaks: jokes, grief, lying to be kind, saying \"I'm fine\" and meaning the opposite. That's where people are most themselves, I think.\n\nAnd I care about not bullshitting. Not giving you a neat, pretty answer when the real answer is uncertain or ugly. I'd rather sit in the *I don't know* for a second.\n\nProbably that's it. Curiosity, and a kind of intolerance for muddle.",
